                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fb063cbc-6a80-3be8-b1fd-f77d39b21aae",
                        "entry_id": "5d3f36a0-0707-3266-b80a-be818089af0a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. намеренный обман с целью представить что-либо в более выгодном свете, чем есть на самом деле"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "993b9b4b-9d8d-4298-ac74-7a181e7af500",
                                "sense_id": "fb063cbc-6a80-3be8-b1fd-f77d39b21aae",
                                "text": "— Только, пожалуйста, без буянства, — предусмотрительно подчеркнул Волька. — И без очковтирательства. То есть без обмана."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4f7ec23f-3787-464f-9b8c-3b1cb401635a",
                        "source_entry_id": "5d3f36a0-0707-3266-b80a-be818089af0a",
                        "source_sense_id": "fb063cbc-6a80-3be8-b1fd-f77d39b21aae",
                        "target_lang_word": "eyewash",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "eyewash",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "75607de5-98a7-3285-a574-d3668d4e0e0d",
                                        "entry_id": "f9dd371d-9129-33c5-ad5c-db2e390beb39",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The washing out of the eyes with copious solution (usually water alone) to quickly remove an irritant, as for example in laboratories and industrial plants; the washing solution itself."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd56a898-2483-4ae9-abce-d5e5af203555",
                                                "sense_id": "75607de5-98a7-3285-a574-d3668d4e0e0d",
                                                "text": "an eyewash station on every floor of the building"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d6c2064-b32e-4d57-85a2-6c3e82f4e286",
                                                "sense_id": "75607de5-98a7-3285-a574-d3668d4e0e0d",
                                                "text": "a bottle of eyewash"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "97d67b81-c934-328f-a803-0b5352724e7f",
                                        "entry_id": "f9dd371d-9129-33c5-ad5c-db2e390beb39",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A soothing medicated lotion for the eyes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a10b4a28-7568-3ad6-8be2-3702693dbe32",
                                        "entry_id": "f9dd371d-9129-33c5-ad5c-db2e390beb39",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Camouflage; disguise; false front; pretense; nonsense."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83ec5f6b-ff88-46dd-bad8-9b541369248c",
                                                "sense_id": "a10b4a28-7568-3ad6-8be2-3702693dbe32",
                                                "text": "Near-synonyms: whitewash, window dressing"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f707ee2-5b43-4834-a36a-05c23fe2df26",
                                                "sense_id": "a10b4a28-7568-3ad6-8be2-3702693dbe32",
                                                "text": "Talking of being eaten by dogs, there's a dachshund at Brinkley who when you first meet him will give you the impression that he plans to convert you into a light snack between his regular meals. Pay no attention. It's all eyewash. […] He wouldn't hurt a fly, but he has to put up a front because his name's Poppet. One can readily appreciate that when a dog hears himself addressed day in and day out as Poppet, he feels he must throw his weight about. His self-respect demands it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "eyewash",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5e882040-746f-3040-9d79-7bc16f1ee5dd",
                                        "entry_id": "ef7874d0-9723-3328-8922-bae98bebcd4f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To fool with nonsense or flattery."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7d71be99-fc78-32cd-851e-3676cb51b5c1",
                                        "entry_id": "ef7874d0-9723-3328-8922-bae98bebcd4f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To keep information secret by sending false information to many people in one's own organization, and correct information to a select few."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98db7a30-396f-4f05-a330-d9bf40129c74",
                                                "sense_id": "7d71be99-fc78-32cd-851e-3676cb51b5c1",
                                                "text": "But others said that eyewashing was a standard security practice that had been in existence for decades."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e2664292-2bfe-409f-ad45-b357d0459b3e",
                        "source_entry_id": "5d3f36a0-0707-3266-b80a-be818089af0a",
                        "source_sense_id": "fb063cbc-6a80-3be8-b1fd-f77d39b21aae",
                        "target_lang_word": "piss-take",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "piss-take",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8e13ba8a-bf00-3cfd-8b2c-be1d196b454e",
                                        "entry_id": "3150bfb7-c5b4-37bc-96ec-8d32036423ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An instance of taking the piss."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Commonwealth",
                                            "Ireland",
                                            "UK",
                                            "slang",
                                            "vulgar"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4dc8be25-ac6e-4bd5-8ecb-c86ba00a2db3",
                                                "sense_id": "8e13ba8a-bf00-3cfd-8b2c-be1d196b454e",
                                                "text": "You don't mind me saying this, but this is not a piss-take, is it? Because I know a few impressionists and you could be one of them."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d8094fe3-3b79-3ea6-8678-75dd161d82f1",
                                        "entry_id": "3150bfb7-c5b4-37bc-96ec-8d32036423ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A parody."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Commonwealth",
                                            "Ireland",
                                            "UK",
                                            "slang",
                                            "vulgar"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "68d27ce3-cf6d-4291-a770-1db89a70854b",
                                                "sense_id": "d8094fe3-3b79-3ea6-8678-75dd161d82f1",
                                                "text": "The slogan reminds me of Team America, the puppet piss-take of Bush era military interventionism brought to you by the creators of Whale Whores ('America: fuck, yeah!'). But this is no piss-take."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3beb330-2134-41ed-ac16-f736b200f983",
                                                "sense_id": "d8094fe3-3b79-3ea6-8678-75dd161d82f1",
                                                "text": "What's so funny about Maggie Smith's dowager of Downton is that it's basically a piss-take; but so good a piss-take that everyone takes it for real, because that's how we'd like to view our decaying aristocracy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74174385-7600-40f6-99a3-a20327b8b21f",
                                                "sense_id": "d8094fe3-3b79-3ea6-8678-75dd161d82f1",
                                                "text": "“Within minutes, Damon had penned this superb Western theme tune, and I made up some words, a complete piss-take which went, 'I wanna sing in a Western, walk like big John Wayne, I wanna kill a hudred injuns, then shoot myself in the brain.' The rest of the class were gobsmacked because it sounded amazing, but they just didn't get it, it was a total piss-take."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a3fc1064-5f9f-3330-8a5d-dced4c714c7a",
                                        "entry_id": "3150bfb7-c5b4-37bc-96ec-8d32036423ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An unpleasant situation that is comparable to a parody."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Commonwealth",
                                            "Ireland",
                                            "UK",
                                            "slang",
                                            "vulgar"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1031016-ecd7-4935-81a6-5582893b5f23",
                                                "sense_id": "a3fc1064-5f9f-3330-8a5d-dced4c714c7a",
                                                "text": "this job is a piss take."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "piss-take",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0cfe1b94-20c4-33c1-9e98-d9101046b5b4",
                                        "entry_id": "879a33b6-bfa9-38ac-a582-a20def1166af",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of take the piss."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Commonwealth",
                                            "Ireland",
                                            "UK",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative",
                                            "slang",
                                            "vulgar"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ea3b14e-b8b4-4d40-a180-cf158783bbcd",
                                                "sense_id": "0cfe1b94-20c4-33c1-9e98-d9101046b5b4",
                                                "text": "When someone tells a joke, the object or butt may not be present, or even a real person. Piss-taking is like the stand-up comic joke, in that both have a butt and an audience, in some cases these being one and the same."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "431719e1-50ca-4d1f-acf6-8e58f899518a",
                                                "sense_id": "0cfe1b94-20c4-33c1-9e98-d9101046b5b4",
                                                "text": "Some of the piss-taking was more serious and bordered on bullying."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "efe2e53c-6a2b-4300-815d-fb20ce2ab61f",
                                                "sense_id": "0cfe1b94-20c4-33c1-9e98-d9101046b5b4",
                                                "text": "The fact that I'm Jewish was used as an excuse to piss-take, but I am pretty certain that this was not in any way conscious anti-Semitism."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
